option.RT_BLOCK_LIGHTS=Ray Tracing
option.RT_BLOCK_LIGHTS.comment=The voxel copy of the world everything is traced through: shadows, block light, path traced light, reflections. Off: no shadows at all.
option.RT_LIGHT_TRACES=Traced Lights Per Pixel
option.RT_LIGHT_TRACES.comment=How many nearby lights get a shadow ray. Higher is more accurate in busy areas but slower.
option.PATH_TRACED_SHADOWS=Path Traced Shadows
option.PATH_TRACED_SHADOWS.comment=Every shadow is a ray from the surface to a random point on the sun's disk, through the real blocks near you (shapes, leaves, glass colours, water) and plain blocks out to the render distance. Soft where a shadow falls far, sharp where things touch. No shadow map.
option.sunPathRotation=Sun Angle
option.SUBSURFACE_SCATTERING=Foliage Subsurface Scattering
option.HAND_LIGHT=Held Item Light
option.AMBIENT_STRENGTH=Sky Light Strength
option.BLOCKLIGHT_STRENGTH=Block Light Strength
option.EMISSIVE_STRENGTH=Emissive Strength

option.WATER_WAVES=Waves
option.WAVE_HEIGHT=Wave Height
option.WAVE_SPEED=Wave Speed
option.INTERACTIVE_RIPPLES=Interactive Ripples
option.INTERACTIVE_RIPPLES.comment=Players, mobs and boats leave ripples and wakes on water. Entity ripples need Shadows on.
option.RIPPLE_STRENGTH=Ripple Strength
option.RAIN_RIPPLES=Rain Ripples
option.WATER_REFRACTION=Refraction
option.REFRACTION_STRENGTH=Refraction Strength
option.WATER_CAUSTICS=Caustics
option.CAUSTIC_STRENGTH=Caustic Strength
option.WATER_CLARITY=Water Clarity

option.SSR=Ray Traced Reflections
option.SSR_STEPS=Reflection Ray Steps
option.RAIN_PUDDLES=Wet Surfaces & Puddles
option.PUDDLE_AMOUNT=Puddle Amount
option.PBR_SPECULAR=PBR Specular (labPBR)
option.NORMAL_MAPPING=Normal Mapping (labPBR)
option.WAVING_PLANTS=Waving Plants
option.PLANT_BENDING=Plants Bend Under You
option.PLANT_BENDING.comment=Grass, flowers, crops and leaves are pushed aside by players, mobs and animals moving through them, and spring back after. Mobs need Shadows on.
option.WAVING_SPEED=Wind Speed

option.VOLUMETRIC_LIGHT=Volumetric Light (God Rays)
option.VL_STEPS=Volumetric Light Steps
option.VL_DENSITY=Volumetric Light Density
option.VOLUMETRIC_CLOUDS=Volumetric Clouds
option.VOLUMETRIC_CLOUDS.comment=Layered cumulus, altocumulus and cirrus, rendered at half resolution with temporal smoothing.
option.CLOUD_STEPS=Cloud Quality
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE=Cloud Coverage
option.CLOUD_ALTITUDE=Cloud Altitude
option.ALTOCUMULUS_CLOUDS=Altocumulus Layer
option.ALTOCUMULUS_CLOUDS.comment=Thin patchy mid-level clouds above the cumulus.
option.CIRRUS_CLOUDS=Cirrus Layer
option.CIRRUS_CLOUDS.comment=Wispy high-altitude streaks.
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS=Cloud Shadows
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS.comment=Clouds cast moving shadows on the ground, water and god rays.
option.STARS=Stars
option.FOG_DENSITY=Fog Density

option.BLOOM=Bloom
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH=Bloom Strength
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE=Auto Exposure
option.EXPOSURE_BIAS=Exposure
option.SATURATION=Saturation
option.CONTRAST=Contrast
option.VIGNETTE=Vignette
option.VIGNETTE_STRENGTH=Vignette Strength
option.FXAA=FXAA
option.SHARPENING=Sharpening

option.MILKY_WAY=Milky Way
option.MILKY_WAY.comment=A band of diffuse starlight with dark dust lanes, turning with the stars.
option.SHOOTING_STARS=Shooting Stars
option.AURORA=Aurora
option.AURORA.comment=Glowing green and purple curtains on clear nights in snowy biomes.
option.AURORA_ALWAYS=Aurora In Every Biome
option.RAINBOW=Rainbows
option.RAINBOW.comment=A rainbow opposite the sun as rain clears.
option.LIGHTNING_FLASH=Lightning Flashes
option.LIGHTNING_FLASH.comment=Lightning strikes light up the sky, clouds and landscape.
option.SURF_FOAM=Shoreline Foam
option.EMISSIVE_ORES=Emissive Ores
option.EMISSIVE_ORES.comment=Off by default: real ores don't glow. The coloured flecks in ores glow faintly in dark caves.
option.PURKINJE=Night Vision Shift
option.PURKINJE.comment=Like real eyes, very dark scenes lose colour and shift towards blue.
option.RT_SUN_SOFTNESS.comment=How big the sun's disk is for the shadow rays: bigger gives softer shadow edges. The real sun is 0.008.
option.RT_SUN_SOFTNESS=Sun Size
option.PATH_TRACING=Path Tracing
option.PATH_TRACING.comment=Light from the sky, sunlit and torch-lit blocks and glowing blocks is path traced through the voxel world: real sky occlusion indoors and under trees, coloured light bouncing between blocks. Averaged over frames and denoised.
option.LENS_FLARE=Lens Flare
option.LENS_FLARE.comment=Glow, streak and ghosts when looking towards the sun; hidden behind terrain and clouds.
option.TAA=Temporal Anti-Aliasing
option.TAA.comment=Smooth edges and noise-free ray traced soft shadows, AO and reflections by combining several jittered frames. Replaces FXAA when on.
option.RT_SHADOW_SOFTNESS=Block Light Shadow Softness
option.FXAA.comment=Only used when TAA is off.
option.CURVED_WORLD=Curved Planet
option.CURVED_WORLD.comment=The world curves away with distance like a small planet. Stays flat while Voxy is running: Voxy doesn't let shaders move LOD terrain.
option.CURVATURE_RADIUS=Planet Radius
option.CURVATURE_RADIUS.comment=Smaller planets curve away sooner. With Distant Horizons the radius is at least 8000 blocks, otherwise the horizon would hide every LOD.
option.SNOW_COVER=Snow Build-up
option.SNOW_COVER.comment=While it snows in snowy biomes, snow collects on upward surfaces and slowly melts after.
option.BIOME_FOG=Biome Fog
option.BIOME_FOG.comment=Thicker haze in humid biomes, warm dust in deserts and badlands, pale haze in snowy biomes.
option.SKY_HALOS=Halos and Sun Dogs
option.SKY_HALOS.comment=On some days (more often in cold biomes) ice crystals make a 22-degree ring round the sun and moon, and bright sun dogs beside a low sun.
option.LENS_RAIN=Rain On The Lens
option.LENS_RAIN.comment=Raindrops land on the screen and run down it while you're outside in the rain.
option.HEAT_HAZE=Heat Haze
option.HEAT_HAZE.comment=Distant terrain shimmers in the Nether and on hot, dry days.
option.DEPTH_OF_FIELD=Depth of Field
option.DEPTH_OF_FIELD.comment=Autofocus on what you're looking at; nearer and farther things blur.
option.DOF_STRENGTH=Depth of Field Strength
option.MOTION_BLUR=Motion Blur
option.MOTION_BLUR_STRENGTH=Motion Blur Strength
option.CHROMATIC_ABERRATION=Chromatic Aberration
option.FILM_GRAIN=Film Grain
option.SPAWN_WARNING=Mob Spawn Warning
option.SPAWN_WARNING.comment=While you hold a light source, floors within 24 blocks where monsters can spawn (block light 0) show a red X.
option.VITALS_FX=Health & Air Effects
option.VITALS_FX.comment=Low health drains colour with a pulsing red heartbeat, damage flashes the edges, and running out of air underwater closes in your view.
option.SNEAK_ZOOM=Zoom While Sneaking
option.SNEAK_ZOOM.comment=Also zoom while sneaking. The zoom key itself comes from the Iris Extension mod: bind "Zoom" to C in Controls. Zooming narrows the field of view, so the world is drawn at full detail; the mouse keeps its normal speed (shaders can't change it).
option.ZOOM_FACTOR=Zoom Amount
option.WET_LENS=Wet Lens After Swimming
option.WET_LENS.comment=Water runs down the screen for a few seconds after you surface.
option.COLD_BREATH=Frosty Breath
option.COLD_BREATH.comment=In snowy biomes you can see your breath.
option.FOOTPRINTS=Snow Footprints
option.FOOTPRINTS=Snow & Sand Tracks
option.FOOTPRINTS.comment=Players, villagers, animals and mobs press real tracks into snow and sand where their bodies touch it: footprints, trails, packed paths, soft rims of pushed-aside powder. Tracks stay where they are and only fill back in while it snows.
option.SNOW_GEOMETRY=3D Snow
option.SNOW_GEOMETRY.comment=Snow near you is real geometry: wind drifts, mounds and lumps, pressed tracks, casting real shadows. The block surface takes over further away.
option.ECLIPSES=Solar Eclipses
option.ECLIPSES.comment=Every 16th day at noon the moon crosses the sun: daylight fades, stars come out and the corona glows.
option.BLOOD_MOON=Blood Moons
option.BLOOD_MOON.comment=Some full moons turn deep red and tint the night.
option.METEOR_SHOWERS=Meteor Showers
option.METEOR_SHOWERS.comment=Every 7th night shooting stars fall constantly.
option.FOG_DENSITY=Fog Density
option.FOG_DENSITY.comment=Distance haze. 0 turns it off (the default).
iris_extension.keybind.key0.name=Flashlight
iris_extension.keybind.key1.name=Zoom (hold)
option.FLASHLIGHT_STRENGTH=Flashlight Brightness
option.FLASHLIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=The flashlight is switched with its key (Iris Extension mod: Options > Controls > Key Binds > Flashlight). It lights blocks and mobs, casts path traced shadows and glints on water and shiny blocks.
option.WATER_GEOMETRY=3D Water
option.WATER_GEOMETRY.comment=Water near you is a fine mesh moved by the real waves, ripples and wakes (geometry shader). Off: flat water with the same lighting.
option.WATER_FOAM=Foam
option.WATER_FOAM.comment=Foam where real water makes it: whitecaps on windy open water, flowing water, splashes and fast swimming. It bursts within seconds.
option.FOAM_AMOUNT=Foam Amount
option.SURF_FOAM.comment=Waves breaking on shores they are big enough to break on (none at a pool's edge), coming and going with the swell.
option.PLANT_BEND_STRENGTH=Plant Bend Strength
option.IBL=Image-Based Lighting
option.IBL.comment=Light from the real surroundings: every frame the world around you (traced through the blocks), the sky and the clouds are captured into an HDR environment map, blurred for each roughness (GGX) and turned into diffuse light. Rough and glossy surfaces reflect it, everything is lit by it beyond the path traced range, and reflections fall back to it where their rays miss.
option.PBR_FORMAT=PBR Format
option.PBR_FORMAT.comment=How your resource pack stores its materials. LabPBR 1.3: almost every current PBR pack (plain RGB normal maps are recognised automatically). Old PBR: SEUS-era packs (smoothness, metalness, emission in the specular map).
value.PBR_FORMAT.0=LabPBR 1.3
value.PBR_FORMAT.1=Old PBR
option.INTEGRATED_PBR=Integrated Materials
option.INTEGRATED_PBR.comment=Where your pack has no specular map, Mist's own materials: ore flecks with their mineral's real gloss and reflectance (gold and copper metallic, diamond brilliant, coal and lapis dull) apart from the stone around them, and metal, gem, quartz and ice blocks.
option.PARALLAX=Parallax (POM)
option.PARALLAX.comment=Real depth in textures: the texture is ray marched against its height so bricks, cobbles and studs hide each other at grazing angles and shade themselves.
option.POM_DEPTH=Parallax Depth
option.POM_DEPTH.comment=How deep the deepest parts of a height map go, in blocks.
option.POM_DISTANCE=Parallax Distance
option.POM_DISTANCE.comment=Out to how many blocks textures get parallax.
option.GENERATED_PARALLAX=Integrated Parallax (iPOM)
option.GENERATED_PARALLAX.comment=Depth for rock, stone bricks, cobblestone, ores, dirt, sand, gravel and the like when your pack has no height maps (vanilla or plain packs): heights from each texture's own shading (darker cracks and gaps lie deeper; bricks with light mortar the other way round), with matching self-shadows and lighting. Packs with their own normal maps are left as made.
option.POM_STEPS=Parallax Quality
option.POM_STEPS.comment=Most steps a view ray takes through a texture's depth (fewer facing it head on, all of them at grazing angles). Higher removes stepping on deep textures, at more cost.
option.SPLASH_SIMULATION=Splash Simulation (MLS-MPM)
option.SPLASH_SIMULATION.comment=Falling or jumping into water runs a real fluid simulation of the water around the impact (Moving Least Squares Material Point Method, up to 32768 water particles on a grid, on the GPU): your body shoves the water into a crater and a crown, spray flies and falls back, the crater closes into a jet, and the rings run out over the water. Stronger and higher the faster you hit it. Costs nothing when nothing splashes.
option.SMOOTH_TERRAIN=Smooth Terrain
option.SMOOTH_TERRAIN.comment=Natural ground (grass, dirt, stone, sand, gravel...) without blocky corners: slopes and rounded hills; plants on it go along. Buildings and paths keep their edges. Needs the Mist Iris Extension mod, which gives shaders each block's neighbours; without it nothing changes.
option.SMOOTH_STRENGTH=Smoothing
option.SMOOTH_STRENGTH.comment=How far the corners move towards the smooth surface (1 = all the way).
